(534234, 52917, 2281, '<td valign="top">Funny, I just called it a Christmas Pickle without knowing the history behind it. Only after people started commenting on it that I found some information out.<br/> <br/>As Harz pointed out it''s an American tradition. Supposedly all the stories of it being a German tradition, finding it for a lucky or special prize was all made up just to increase revenue. Actual Germans know nothing about the tradition, even glass blowers in Germany that make Christmas decorations.<br/> <br/>This one was given to us by my girlfriends parents. This was one of many glass blown decorations in a very large box of glass fruits, veggies, dolls and other various Christmas themes. We hang this one on the fish tank where our fish "Mr. Pickles" lives.</td>', 'Funny, I just called it a Christmas Pickle without knowing the history behind it. Only after people started commenting on it that I found some information out. As Harz pointed out it''s an American tradition. Supposedly all the stories of it being a German tradition, finding it for a lucky or special prize was all made up just to increase revenue. Actual Germans know nothing about the tradition, even glass blowers in Germany that make Christmas decorations. This one was given to us by my girlfriends parents. This was one of many glass blown decorations in a very large box of glass fruits, veggies, dolls and other various Christmas themes. We hang this one on the fish tank where our fish "Mr. Pickles" lives.', '2004-01-07 03:08:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(534239, 52583, 5158, '<td valign="top">Wuhu!<br/>I''m very excited to get a ribbon on this on, especially because Kaja was pretty sad after her Clichés entry didn''t work so well.<br/>She will get a nice and tasty bone tonight.<br/>She as well as I says thanks to all commenter and voters of course.<br/> <br/>I''m also excited to get a ribbon in a challenge where I''m still not sure about the meaning of it: the phrase "tacky" isn''t clear to me still.<br/>I knew that the 1st and 2nd placed pictures are right on the intention of the challenge, but was mine?!<br/>Anyhow, was a lot of fun to make the image and I was of course lucky that I pressed the shutter at this very moment shown in the image.<br/> <br/>So thanx again to everybody on this great site,<br/> <br/>Jörg</td>', 'Wuhu!I''m very excited to get a ribbon on this on, especially because Kaja was pretty sad after her Clichés entry didn''t work so well.She will get a nice and tasty bone tonight.She as well as I says thanks to all commenter and voters of course. I''m also excited to get a ribbon in a challenge where I''m still not sure about the meaning of it: the phrase "tacky" isn''t clear to me still.I knew that the 1st and 2nd placed pictures are right on the intention of the challenge, but was mine?!Anyhow, was a lot of fun to make the image and I was of course lucky that I pressed the shutter at this very moment shown in the image. So thanx again to everybody on this great site, Jörg', '2004-01-07 03:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(534243, 52235, 5158, '<td valign="top">Congrats for your very tacky shot (although I''m still not sure about the translation to German).<br/>Was one of my favorits and I knew it was impossible to beat: right on the intention of the challenge and very well made!<br/>Thumb up!<br/> <br/>Of course you have to go to the families living in the house and congrat them too!!</td>', 'Congrats for your very tacky shot (although I''m still not sure about the translation to German).Was one of my favorits and I knew it was impossible to beat: right on the intention of the challenge and very well made!Thumb up! Of course you have to go to the families living in the house and congrat them too!!', '2004-01-07 03:17:01.000000', NULL, 0),
