(534942, 52586, 14476, '<td valign="top">This was a good try!  Keep it up.  One thought - some commenters have recommended using a tripod and that is best.  When a tripod is just not practical like in a car, you might rig up a "beanbag."  This can be made with a large bag filled about 3/4 with beans, or almost anything with "just enough" give/firmness to it to steady your camera.  Drape this over the car window and you''re in business. (My beanbag is a pillow case filled with a couple of old rolled up blankets.)</td>', 'This was a good try!  Keep it up.  One thought - some commenters have recommended using a tripod and that is best.  When a tripod is just not practical like in a car, you might rig up a "beanbag."  This can be made with a large bag filled about 3/4 with beans, or almost anything with "just enough" give/firmness to it to steady your camera.  Drape this over the car window and you''re in business. (My beanbag is a pillow case filled with a couple of old rolled up blankets.)', '2004-01-07 13:17:59.000000', NULL, 0),
