(541457, 52587, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>This photo doesn''t really appear to meet the challege in my opinion.  It is a ''christmas'' photograph, but it os not really a decoration.  I don''t find anything particularly tacky or gaudy about it.  It is out of focus as well.  I don''t know if this was your intent, but it does add some amount of an interesting mood.  My overall opinion of this photo is that it is subjectively weak for use in a challenge here.  <br/> <br/>Better luck next time :)<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... This photo doesn''t really appear to meet the challege in my opinion.  It is a ''christmas'' photograph, but it os not really a decoration.  I don''t find anything particularly tacky or gaudy about it.  It is out of focus as well.  I don''t know if this was your intent, but it does add some amount of an interesting mood.  My overall opinion of this photo is that it is subjectively weak for use in a challenge here.   Better luck next time :)', '2004-01-13 19:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(541597, 52344, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Wow this is the first time I''ve drawn a shot that has NO comments previously...<br/> <br/>First let me say that I love the color tone here.  Nice shadings of red complimented with the warm hues of the light bulbs!<br/> <br/>This shot seems to suffer from a lack of focus in more ways than one.  There doesn''t seem to be any one spot in the shot that is really in focus.  If you were shooting for a soft focus effect you ALMOST have it, but there doesn''t seem to be a reason for it.<br/> <br/>From a compositional point of view there is no subjective focus point here.  There isn''t a real place to look.  There seems to be no real singular purpose for the shot.  The shot is also (wierdly enough) kind of busy in a simple kind of way.  There are a few too many competing lines trying to draw your attention to a non existant focal point...<br/> <br/>One thing that you did do <i>exceptionally</i> well in my opinion was the exposure on the lights.  It is right on without being over exposed at all!<br/> <br/>Don''t let the low score get ya down because I''m looking forward to seeing more of your work!<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club Wow this is the first time I''ve drawn a shot that has NO comments previously... First let me say that I love the color tone here.  Nice shadings of red complimented with the warm hues of the light bulbs! This shot seems to suffer from a lack of focus in more ways than one.  There doesn''t seem to be any one spot in the shot that is really in focus.  If you were shooting for a soft focus effect you ALMOST have it, but there doesn''t seem to be a reason for it. From a compositional point of view there is no subjective focus point here.  There isn''t a real place to look.  There seems to be no real singular purpose for the shot.  The shot is also (wierdly enough) kind of busy in a simple kind of way.  There are a few too many competing lines trying to draw your attention to a non existant focal point... One thing that you did do exceptionally well in my opinion was the exposure on the lights.  It is right on without being over exposed at all! Don''t let the low score get ya down because I''m looking forward to seeing more of your work!TC', '2004-01-13 23:17:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(541630, 52583, 6477, '<td valign="top">I like very much the idea, composition and everything, but the top ten model is who took the credit without a doubt:))) I hope you gave Kaja a big raw meaty bone! :)</td>', 'I like very much the idea, composition and everything, but the top ten model is who took the credit without a doubt:))) I hope you gave Kaja a big raw meaty bone! :)', '2004-01-13 23:51:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(542266, 52820, 1570, '<td valign="top">i thought this picture was simply incredible... sorry, i didn''t have a chance to comment on it during the challenge, but i did give it one of the two tens!it''s in my favorites now...</td>', 'i thought this picture was simply incredible... sorry, i didn''t have a chance to comment on it during the challenge, but i did give it one of the two tens!it''s in my favorites now...', '2004-01-14 09:43:29.000000', NULL, 0),
